ok   event: one server answers on TCP and on a unix socket
ok   event: the unix socket gets the requested mode
ok   event: shutdown removes the unix socket file
ok   base: one server answers on TCP and on a unix socket
ok   base: the unix socket gets the requested mode
ok   base: shutdown removes the unix socket file
ok   event: a listening descriptor handed over is served
ok   base: a listening descriptor named as fd:N is served
ok   listen strings name TCP and unix addresses
ok   a stale unix socket file is left behind by a dead server
ok   a stale unix socket file is replaced
ok   a unix socket that still accepts is not taken over
ok   event: shutdown does not unlink a replacement unix socket
ok   base: shutdown does not unlink a replacement unix socket
ok   reuse_port lets two servers bind one port
ok   a second listener on a taken port reports the address
ok   reuse_port cannot use an ephemeral port
ok   base also refuses ephemeral reuse_port
ok   workers option is no longer available
ok   buffer_body cannot exceed max_body on event
ok   buffer_body cannot exceed max_body on base
ok   Listen.systemd is empty without LISTEN_FDS
ok   Listen.parse reads an IPv6 address
ok   listen needs a port
ok   backlog must be positive
ok   max_connection_rate must not be negative
ok   base refuses TLS
ok   TLS refuses unsupported h2 ALPN
ok   TLS refuses mixed supported and unsupported ALPN
ok   TLS accepts HTTP/1.1 ALPN
ok   TLS refuses empty ALPN
